# An operator at the start of a line without a pipe: one error, then it parses as an operator.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where x > 1
project a
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..26
  PIPELINE@0..25
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..15
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..15
        NAME_REF@10..11
          IDENT@10..11 "x"
        WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
        GT@12..13 ">"
        WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
        LITERAL@14..15
          LONG@14..15 "1"
    WHITESPACE@15..16 "\n"
    PROJECT_OP@16..25
      IDENT@16..23 "project"
      WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@24..25
        NAME_REF@24..25
          IDENT@24..25 "a"
  WHITESPACE@25..26 "\n"

error[DS0102]: missing `|` before `project`
  --> query:2:1
  |
2 | project a
  | ^^^^^^^ `project` starts a new operator
  |
  = help: insert `|` to pipe into `project`: `| project`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    t | where x > 1
    | project a
which parses without errors
